    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T20:24:44Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main e048b103c: concurrent_headless_starts_finish_without_a_native_crash passes without a change. Suggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n\nThe temporary pin starts three headless runs together. All 10 test runs passed, for 30 headless calls. No production code changed. I could not reproduce SIGSEGV on Linux. This result does not establish the cause of the intermittent crash.\n\nThe three tests that did not report in the failed run were egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero, a_headless_start_with_a_model_file_imports_and_draws_it, and a_headless_start_with_a_project_file_opens_and_draws_it. All three create a GPU device. The five completed tests return before GPU creation.\n\nRun 44596948231 is still pending. I found no commit that establishes a fix. Commit 16a4f3be5 fixed an earlier world initialization race, but it predates the failed run.\n\nSTOPPED: the pin passed on unchanged code. Claim released. No fix or PR was made.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
